(7735515, 1274984, 29535, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Neat:</b></div><hr/><i> Congratulations on your first ribbon with a lovely serene shot. It''s funny on first view this reminded me of a similar shot I''ve taken at Lake Garda, which is close by.<br/> <br/>So is this Lake Como? and if so how wonderful if you live there, was just talking about out adventures there yesterday. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thank you! I''m so happy :.) So this isn''t actually Lake Como, I''ve added details to the description above but it''s a smaller lake a short drive from its more famous relative. Once upon a time the two lakes along with Lake Ceresio of Lugano formed one huge body of water before the last ice age.<br/> <br/>I find a lot of inspiration at Lago di Piano as it''s quite wild and has a lot of animals around. However I''m looking to do some shots of Lake Como in these days perhaps for the harbour challenge as there are a fair few to choose from!<br/> <br/>Lake Garda is supposed to be quite similar and very nice, I''ll have to make the trip over there some day!</td>', 'Originally posted by Neat: Congratulations on your first ribbon with a lovely serene shot. It''s funny on first view this reminded me of a similar shot I''ve taken at Lake Garda, which is close by. So is this Lake Como? and if so how wonderful if you live there, was just talking about out adventures there yesterday.   Thank you! I''m so happy :.) So this isn''t actually Lake Como, I''ve added details to the description above but it''s a smaller lake a short drive from its more famous relative. Once upon a time the two lakes along with Lake Ceresio of Lugano formed one huge body of water before the last ice age. I find a lot of inspiration at Lago di Piano as it''s quite wild and has a lot of animals around. However I''m looking to do some shots of Lake Como in these days perhaps for the harbour challenge as there are a fair few to choose from! Lake Garda is supposed to be quite similar and very nice, I''ll have to make the trip over there some day!', '2022-12-26 04:23:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(7735516, 1275048, 29535, '<td valign="top">Congrats on the HM! I find myself coming back to look at this one more than most of the others in the contest, so whilst I stand by my original comments I sense they are evolving somewhat. There is something so captivating about this image and style. Well done!</td>', 'Congrats on the HM! I find myself coming back to look at this one more than most of the others in the contest, so whilst I stand by my original comments I sense they are evolving somewhat. There is something so captivating about this image and style. Well done!', '2022-12-26 04:30:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(7735517, 1275001, 29535, '<td valign="top">Congrats on the ribbon and I''m glad this was my top pick! Also good to see another shooter back after a few years away, great woodland shot and a wonderful landscape!</td>', 'Congrats on the ribbon and I''m glad this was my top pick! Also good to see another shooter back after a few years away, great woodland shot and a wonderful landscape!', '2022-12-26 04:31:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(7735523, 1274891, 29535, '<td valign="top">This was one of my top picks! It was also similar to my original concept before I got lucky spotting the fisherman. Life is funny sometimes. Great shot!</td>', 'This was one of my top picks! It was also similar to my original concept before I got lucky spotting the fisherman. Life is funny sometimes. Great shot!', '2022-12-26 04:58:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(7735524, 1274984, 123833, '<td valign="top">Congrats on the amazing restart after 15 years - first ribbon and a PB! I am sure many more will follow :)</td>', 'Congrats on the amazing restart after 15 years - first ribbon and a PB! I am sure many more will follow :)', '2022-12-26 05:55:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(7735526, 1275048, 117474, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Rankles:</b></div><hr/><i> Congrats on the HM! I find myself coming back to look at this one more than most of the others in the contest, so whilst I stand by my original comments I sense they are evolving somewhat. There is something so captivating about this image and style. Well done! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks :-) I went through a journey that led me to appreciate this style that started by asking "what was the photographer trying to evoke with the editing choices?", and eventually I asked this question so much that it became a core element of my style. This isn''t to say there''s any great depth in my images by any means, but usually I have something that I want to communicate indirectly. Here, for example, the subject is reading a book and the focus and texture is meant to contrast the background noise to his complete focus on the novel. Usually, lighting, focus and textures are used in various combinations for some kind of purpose. <br/> <br/>Anyway, I have a special appreciation of voters'' evolving perception of style, and encourage you down the route whatever the outcome may be!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2022-12-26 08:14:59.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by Rankles: Congrats on the HM! I find myself coming back to look at this one more than most of the others in the contest, so whilst I stand by my original comments I sense they are evolving somewhat. There is something so captivating about this image and style. Well done!   Thanks :-) I went through a journey that led me to appreciate this style that started by asking "what was the photographer trying to evoke with the editing choices?", and eventually I asked this question so much that it became a core element of my style. This isn''t to say there''s any great depth in my images by any means, but usually I have something that I want to communicate indirectly. Here, for example, the subject is reading a book and the focus and texture is meant to contrast the background noise to his complete focus on the novel. Usually, lighting, focus and textures are used in various combinations for some kind of purpose.  Anyway, I have a special appreciation of voters'' evolving perception of style, and encourage you down the route whatever the outcome may be!', '2022-12-26 08:06:59.000000', '2022-12-26 08:14:59.000000', 0),
(7735527, 1274984, 114285, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Rankles:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Neat:</b></div><hr/><i> Congratulations on your first ribbon with a lovely serene shot. It''s funny on first view this reminded me of a similar shot I''ve taken at Lake Garda, which is close by.<br/> <br/>So is this Lake Como? and if so how wonderful if you live there, was just talking about out adventures there yesterday. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thank you! I''m so happy :.) So this isn''t actually Lake Como, I''ve added details to the description above but it''s a smaller lake a short drive from its more famous relative. Once upon a time the two lakes along with Lake Ceresio of Lugano formed one huge body of water before the last ice age.<br/> <br/>I find a lot of inspiration at Lago di Piano as it''s quite wild and has a lot of animals around. However I''m looking to do some shots of Lake Como in these days perhaps for the harbour challenge as there are a fair few to choose from!<br/> <br/>Lake Garda is supposed to be quite similar and very nice, I''ll have to make the trip over there some day! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks for that i started reading your blog but it was way tooo long lol, so I stopped. But thanks for the heads up.</td>', 'Originally posted by Rankles: Originally posted by Neat: Congratulations on your first ribbon with a lovely serene shot. It''s funny on first view this reminded me of a similar shot I''ve taken at Lake Garda, which is close by. So is this Lake Como? and if so how wonderful if you live there, was just talking about out adventures there yesterday.   Thank you! I''m so happy :.) So this isn''t actually Lake Como, I''ve added details to the description above but it''s a smaller lake a short drive from its more famous relative. Once upon a time the two lakes along with Lake Ceresio of Lugano formed one huge body of water before the last ice age. I find a lot of inspiration at Lago di Piano as it''s quite wild and has a lot of animals around. However I''m looking to do some shots of Lake Como in these days perhaps for the harbour challenge as there are a fair few to choose from! Lake Garda is supposed to be quite similar and very nice, I''ll have to make the trip over there some day!   Thanks for that i started reading your blog but it was way tooo long lol, so I stopped. But thanks for the heads up.', '2022-12-26 08:07:24.000000', NULL, 0),
